[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"CI/CD Pipeline Integration for Selenium Automation"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) pipelines are essential for modern software testing. Integrating Selenium test suites into CI/CD tools like Jenkins, GitLab CI, and GitHub Actions ensures that your regression suite runs automatically with every code commit or pull request, providing rapid feedback to the development team."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites for Pipeline Integration"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"A working Selenium test project configured with a build tool like Maven or Gradle."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Test execution capability in a headless browser mode (e.g., Chrome/Firefox headless) since CI runners typically lack a graphical user interface."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"A version control system (Git) repository hosting the source code and test suite."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Jenkins Integration"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Jenkins uses a Jenkinsfile written in Groovy to define the pipeline stages. Below is an example declarative pipeline that checks out code, builds the project, and executes the Selenium tests."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"pipeline {
    agent any
    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git 'https://github.com/your-repo/selenium-project.git'
            }
        }
        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn clean compile'
            }
        }
        stage('Run Selenium Tests') {
            steps {
                sh 'mvn test'
            }
        }
    }
    post {
        always {
            junit 'target/surefire-reports/*.xml'
        }
    }
}"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"2. GitLab CI Integration"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"GitLab CI utilizes a .gitlab-ci.yml file located at the root of your repository. You can use official Maven Docker images to run your Selenium tests inside a containerized runner environment."},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"stages:
  - test

selenium_test_job:
  image: maven:3.8.4-openjdk-11
  stage: test
  script:
    - mvn clean test
  artifacts:
    when: always
    paths:
      - target/surefire-reports/
    reports:
      junit: target/surefire-reports/TEST-*.xml"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"3. GitHub Actions Integration"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"GitHub Actions executes workflows defined in YAML files inside the .github/workflows directory. The following workflow triggers on every push to the main branch and sets up a Java environment to run Maven commands."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"name: Selenium CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [ "main" ]
  pull_request:
    branches: [ "main" ]

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
    - uses: actions/checkout@v3
    - name: Set up JDK 11
      uses: actions/setup-java@v3
      with:
        java-version: '11'
        distribution: 'temurin'
    - name: Run Selenium Tests with Maven
      run: mvn clean test
    - name: Upload Test Results
      uses: actions/upload-artifact@v3
      if: always()
      with:
        name: surefire-reports
        path: target/surefire-reports/"},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Selenium CI/CD Pipelines"},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always configure your WebDriver instance to run in headless mode in CI environments to avoid display-related crashes."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Publish test reports (JUnit XML or Allure reports) to the CI server so stakeholders can review failures without downloading raw logs."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Leverage Docker containers with pre-installed browser drivers to maintain consistency across local and remote test executions."}]
